<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>

        <!--
        AOT smoke test #6: the MARTEN-backed HTTP lane.

        Every other native lane references Wolverine, Wolverine.Http or Wolverine.Sqlite, so no native image
        in CI has ever booted Wolverine.Marten. Three startup failures that only a Marten-backed HTTP app
        reaches therefore shipped in 6.46 (each is masked by the one before it):

          1. SideEffectPolicy cannot find Execute/ExecuteAsync on Wolverine.Marten.IStartStream, so an
             endpoint returning MartenOps.StartStream throws InvalidSideEffectException.
          2. HttpChain.tryApplyAsEndpointMetadataProvider closes HttpChain+Applier<T> over a
             Results<Ok<T>, ProblemHttpResult> return type with CloseAndBuildAs. The closed type is trimmed
             (MissingMethodException, or NotSupportedException "missing native code or metadata"). This is
             not the Configuration.Applier<T> that the GH-4778 rooting block covers.
          3. IntegrateWithWolverine registers Envelope with Schema.For<Envelope>(), and in a native image
             Marten's DocumentMapping cannot find Envelope.Id.

        The endpoint shapes are the ones the reporting application uses. Boots, serves both endpoints and
        reads the started stream back. Needs the postgresql service from docker-compose.yml.

        Refresh the committed pre-gen FROM THIS PROJECT'S DIRECTORY, with Postgres running:

          dotnet run -f net9.0 codegen write

        This project carries NO hand-written roots, so the lane fails until the library itself is fixed.
        -->
        <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
        <StripSymbols>false</StripSymbols>
        <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>

        <!-- Runtime behaviour of a native image is what this asserts; mirrors Wolverine.AotSmoke.Http. -->
        <SuppressTrimAnalysisWarnings>true</SuppressTrimAnalysisWarnings>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IL2026;IL2046;IL2055;IL2065;IL2067;IL2070;IL2072;IL2075;IL2087;IL2090;IL2091;IL2104;IL2111;IL3000;IL3050;IL3051;IL3053</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Http\Wolverine.Http.Marten\Wolverine.Http.Marten.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
